WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.501
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:05.767
You are here. You made it. Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:07.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:11.934
Well, guys, last night was the 65th annual Grammy Awards.

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:14.868
And I -- I love the Grammys.

00:00:14.868 --> 00:00:18.267
Where else can you see Beyoncé and Taylor Swift together?

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:19.868
You know?

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:21.133
Ticketmaster's like,

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:23.968
"We can't even make one of those things happen.

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:27.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.834 --> 00:00:29.267
That's how hard it is."

00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:32.434
This year's Grammy ceremony lasted nearly four hours.

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:34.434
-Ooh. -That's dangerous.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:35.601
I'll tell you why.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:36.934
Because every CBS viewer knows

00:00:36.934 --> 00:00:38.400
that if it lasts longer than four hours,

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.734
they should call their doctor. That's what...

00:00:40.734 --> 00:00:43.167
The Grammys lasted almost four hours,

00:00:43.167 --> 00:00:45.167
although an hour of that was just stalling

00:00:45.167 --> 00:00:47.701
until Beyoncé showed up.

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:49.167
I don't know if you saw this. This was crazy.

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:51.267
Beyoncé couldn't accept her first award

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:54.033
because she was stuck in traffic.

00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:56.367
Yeah, I mean, at this point, I'm surprised she didn't just

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:58.667
get out and part the sea of cars like Moses.

00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:00.367
I mean, it's Beyoncé.

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:02.434
Seriously, if you think your job is stressful,

00:01:02.434 --> 00:01:05.133
imagine being the limo driver who got Beyoncé stuck in traffic

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:08.434
on the night she's making history.

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:11.100
That's right. Beyoncé won her 32nd award,

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:15.167
becoming the most decorated artist in Grammys history.

00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:16.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:18.734
Yep, she's the only person who gets her steps in

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:20.033
at an awards show.

00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:23.234
It's like, "Yep. Yeah. I hit 10,000. There you go."

00:01:23.234 --> 00:01:25.234
Switching gears, everyone's still talking about this.

00:01:25.234 --> 00:01:27.367
Over the weekend, U.S. military fighter jets

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:31.467
shot down a Chinese spy balloon over the Atlantic Ocean.

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:33.334
And this is fun. Instead of a medal,

00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:34.934
the pilot who popped the balloon

00:01:34.934 --> 00:01:37.100
got to pick any stuffed animal on the top shelf.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.467
"I'll take the SpongeB--

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:42.467
You know what? I'll take Bluey. I like Bluey."

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:45.634
Yeah, the balloon floated from Montana to South Carolina.

00:01:45.634 --> 00:01:47.968
Somehow it got across the country faster

00:01:47.968 --> 00:01:50.868
than someone flying Southwest, but it...

00:01:50.868 --> 00:01:52.701
But the U.S. really didn't have a choice.

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:54.734
The only other option was to rub the balloon

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:57.400
on Bernie Sanders and stick it to Canada.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:01.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.567
Some more big news.

00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:03.901
Tomorrow night, President Biden

00:02:03.901 --> 00:02:05.834
will deliver his State of the Union address.

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:08.000
And today he tweeted a photo of his speech

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.534
with the caption, "Getting ready."

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:12.968
Yeah, every time he nails a sentence,

00:02:12.968 --> 00:02:14.467
he gets a cookie, apparently.

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.367 --> 00:02:19.467
"Give him a cookie."

00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:22.100
Apparently, Biden is writing his speech and waiting for Santa.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.367
It's kind of interesting. Some business news.

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:26.634
I saw that next year, Apple could introduce

00:02:26.634 --> 00:02:29.501
a more expensive iPhone called the Ultra.

00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:31.033
-Ooh. -Yep.

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:32.634
This one will have two flashlights

00:02:32.634 --> 00:02:33.968
that turn on in your pocket.

00:02:33.968 --> 00:02:36.801
-Ohh!

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:38.601
-Of course, you've got to take better care

00:02:38.601 --> 00:02:40.033
of a more expensive iPhone.

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:41.501
If you drop this one in the toilet,

00:02:41.501 --> 00:02:44.100
you have to put it in a bowl of risotto.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:46.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.334 --> 00:02:47.734
-Come on! -Thank you, thank you.

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:50.334
♪♪

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:52.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.200
This -- Some movie news.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.067
This weekend, "Knock at the Cabin"

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:59.100
beat "Avatar: The Way of Water" at the box office.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:00.801
Yeah, the movie's a huge success.

00:03:00.801 --> 00:03:02.567
They've already come up with a few sequels.

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:03.834
-Really? -Yeah.

00:03:03.834 --> 00:03:05.767
After "Knock at the Cabin," they're going to release

00:03:05.767 --> 00:03:08.234
"Knock, Knock at the Cabin."

00:03:08.234 --> 00:03:10.667
Then...

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:12.767
Followed by...

00:03:12.767 --> 00:03:15.067
Then...

00:03:15.067 --> 00:03:16.634
Finally...

00:03:19.133 --> 00:03:21.200
"I didn't say banana at the cabin."

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.767
[ Applause ]

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:25.067
Did you guys see this?

00:03:25.067 --> 00:03:27.400
AMC announced that they're going to start charging

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.133
different prices for tickets

00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:30.834
based on where you're sitting in the theater.

00:03:30.834 --> 00:03:32.567
[ Audience groans ]

00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:34.067
I'm not sure about this.

00:03:34.067 --> 00:03:36.200
I mean, it's rough when you're in boarding group D

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:40.901
for "Puss in Boots." You know? You go...

00:03:40.901 --> 00:03:44.200
Some sports news. The Super Bowl is this Sunday.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.501
[ Cheers and applause ] Yeah, that's right.

00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:48.801
-Chiefs!

00:03:48.801 --> 00:03:50.501
-I read that this year the broadcast

00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:53.701
will have even more alcohol ads than usual.

00:03:53.701 --> 00:03:57.934
Finally, a chance to make football fans aware of alcohol.

00:03:57.934 --> 00:04:00.334
Guys, I heard about the founder of Spotify.

00:04:00.334 --> 00:04:03.534
He helped create a body scanner that can detect the growth

00:04:03.534 --> 00:04:06.467
of things like rashes and birthmarks.

00:04:06.467 --> 00:04:08.934
Damn. It sounds like the real Spotify.

00:04:08.934 --> 00:04:12.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.234 --> 00:04:14.868
-Come on!

00:04:14.868 --> 00:04:16.000
Come on! That's two!

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.634
Wow! -Yeah, and this is cool.

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:20.567
At the end of the year, they're going to make

00:04:20.567 --> 00:04:24.901
all your skin tags into a Coachella poster.

00:04:24.901 --> 00:04:26.667
Meanwhile, if your rash has grown,

00:04:26.667 --> 00:04:28.634
the Spotify scanner just plays this.

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:32.801
-♪ You know it's not the same as it was ♪

00:04:32.801 --> 00:04:34.200
[ Applause ]

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.567
Finally, guys, it's Monday, and I think we all could use

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:38.400
a little encouragement to make it through

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.234
the rest of the week. Don't you feel that way?

00:04:40.234 --> 00:04:42.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:45.467
It's time for some "Monday Motivations."

00:04:45.467 --> 00:04:47.167
Here we go.

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:53.067
♪♪

00:04:53.067 --> 00:04:54.934
You look amazing in that shirt.

00:04:57.868 --> 00:05:00.634
Trust me. You're gonna have the best week.

00:05:02.367 --> 00:05:04.300
When you go to the zoo, everyone's like,

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:05.934
"Wow. What a beautiful specimen."

00:05:05.934 --> 00:05:08.601
And they're not talking about the animals.

00:05:10.567 --> 00:05:12.901
On day one of planning her world tour,

00:05:12.901 --> 00:05:16.801
Beyoncé sat down and was like, "So where does Abby live?"

00:05:16.801 --> 00:05:19.501
[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:05:19.501 --> 00:05:21.434
When you agree to see a dessert menu,

00:05:21.434 --> 00:05:23.334
the waiter is like, "Yay. You're staying."

00:05:23.334 --> 00:05:25.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:26.634 --> 00:05:28.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:31.667
[ Laughs ]

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:34.634
You can feel this one?

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:37.734
The day you got your braces off, your orthodontist was like,

00:05:37.734 --> 00:05:40.033
"Oh, God. What if I never see her again?"

00:05:40.033 --> 00:05:43.534
[ Applause ]

00:05:43.534 --> 00:05:46.000
When you get pit stains, everyone's like,

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.501
"A shirt with polka dots in the armpits? I love that."

00:05:48.501 --> 00:05:51.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:53.467
When you click "book flight" online,

00:05:53.467 --> 00:05:55.234
the President of Costa Rica is like,

00:05:55.234 --> 00:05:57.901
"O-M-G, guys! Emily's coming! Emily's coming!"

00:05:57.901 --> 00:06:00.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:00.634 --> 00:06:03.767
And finally, when your phone dies, it's like,

00:06:03.767 --> 00:06:06.801
"My one regret is not spending more time with you."

